                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "634f874e-abde-3901-b8dc-7f07b0a3081c",
                                        "entry_id": "a4fd001b-8840-3b32-b407-a1bf849a4b7e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Derived from one's father."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5099ecaf-7d4e-30ed-b79f-18193d706664",
                                        "entry_id": "a4fd001b-8840-3b32-b407-a1bf849a4b7e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Derived from one's ancestors."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ede3cef-fa16-4fbb-b81e-202ce5aed92b",
                                                "sense_id": "5099ecaf-7d4e-30ed-b79f-18193d706664",
                                                "text": "a patronymic denomination"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85bfdad7-f3ee-440d-8375-0eb84d73452b",
                                                "sense_id": "5099ecaf-7d4e-30ed-b79f-18193d706664",
                                                "text": "I proposed to her that we give our first-born baby a patronymic name."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "patronymic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ad151300-37cb-379c-8f0e-e45b91667abe",
                                        "entry_id": "c58dfe22-5acc-3257-a90c-f4c745882858",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A name acquired from one's father."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "563a9b5a-716b-377c-b37c-41f509f2e93b",
                                        "entry_id": "c58dfe22-5acc-3257-a90c-f4c745882858",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A name acquired from the first name of one's father, grandfather or earlier (male) ancestor. Some cultures use a patronymic where other cultures use a surname or family name; other cultures (like Russia) use both a patronymic and a surname."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41cc543e-d34a-40de-b119-c871d14e71b0",
                                                "sense_id": "563a9b5a-716b-377c-b37c-41f509f2e93b",
                                                "text": "The use of patronymics arose early in Russia, and they continue to be used down to the present day, through proper surnames came into use in the Middle Ages."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7edc4c4c-1f98-485a-8c22-019c363932ad",
                                                "sense_id": "563a9b5a-716b-377c-b37c-41f509f2e93b",
                                                "text": "According to the applicant, for many years she had been living as part of a family with her stepfather, mother and half-brother and wanted to associate herself more closely with them by taking the surname of her stepfather and also a patronymic derived from his forename.\nOn 24 March 2004 the applicant lodged a request with the Civil Status Registration Office in Bila Tserkva (hereinafter “the Registration Office”) seeking to change her patronymic from Volodymyrivna (Володимирівна) to Yuriyivna (Юріївна).\nBy a letter of 27 March 2004 the Registration Office refused the applicant’s request, referring to the Rules on Civil Status Registration in Ukraine, approved by the Ministry of Justice, which provided that the patronymic of a physical person could only be changed in the event of a change of forename by his or her father.\nOn 23 April 2004 the applicant challenged this refusal in the Bila Tserkva Local Court. She complained that her patronymic, along with her forename and family name, was part of her full name and she had the right to change it. She maintained that the refusal violated her constitutional rights, was unconstitutional and was not based on law. She further contended that she had good reasons for changing her patronymic - to disassociate herself from her biological father and associate herself more closely with her stepfather and half-brother."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2a84de9b-bf8b-4c66-ba2b-6ddbae8a4fe6",
                        "source_entry_id": "44c11d76-e37e-3763-afac-8298f2380b23",
                        "source_sense_id": "ecd40381-ed05-3a79-9d76-50f84e05a344",
                        "source_sense_description": "Vorname des Vaters als Namensbestandteil seines Kindes",
                        "target_lang_word": "patronyme",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "patronyme",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4d5f4ef2-63df-3c27-831e-b51780987954",
                                        "entry_id": "29c4599e-8b20-3e89-8a97-6b91092a298f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Nom dérivé du prénom du père, dans certaines traditions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "note": "Quand il existe en parallèle un nom de famille, le patronyme s’énonce en général entre le prénom et le nom de famille",
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fd968f3-ab98-4be6-956a-f6b09bbc77a7",
                                                "sense_id": "4d5f4ef2-63df-3c27-831e-b51780987954",
                                                "text": "Le russe a un système particulier de nom en trois parties : prénom, patronyme (nom du père), et nom de famille."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8e4e0adc-948c-3a76-a06e-d8184e7c76ea",
                                        "entry_id": "29c4599e-8b20-3e89-8a97-6b91092a298f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Nom de famille hérité du père."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd260c8e-4f46-4a1d-8bea-5628bb3f6cc8",
                                                "sense_id": "8e4e0adc-948c-3a76-a06e-d8184e7c76ea",
                                                "text": "Un homme d’honneur était prêt à tout pour préserver son patronyme de l’opprobre."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd171f8f-61e7-4387-9d97-8306dac6d869",
                                                "sense_id": "8e4e0adc-948c-3a76-a06e-d8184e7c76ea",
                                                "text": "La plupart des patronymes se répétaient et se ressemblaient, à croire que ces gens vivaient tous en cousinage. Mais ce n’était qu’un faux-semblant, le postier de Péronville l’avait bien avertie là-dessus."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a6016069-b663-4067-a7f2-a1d5c790d50f",
                        "source_entry_id": "44c11d76-e37e-3763-afac-8298f2380b23",
